        "mission_intent": "We need to stand up a dedicated collection posture focused on the India-Pakistan bilateral dynamic, specifically monitoring for potential crisis triggers that could lead to rapid escalation between New Delhi and Islamabad. The 2024 threat assessment highlights that while the 2021 Line of Control ceasefire holds, neither side has used the calm period to meaningfully rebuild ties, and Pakistan's ongoing support to anti-India militant networks combined with PM Modi's demonstrated willingness to respond with military force creates a volatile backdrop. I want the South Asia desk to task SIGINT and HUMINT assets to provide early warning on any provocative cross-border militant activity, unusual military posturing along the LoC and the International Boundary, and shifts in Pakistani security establishment messaging regarding India. Coordinate with DIA and NSA/CSS to deconflict collection efforts and ensure we have adequate technical coverage of key command-and-control nodes on both sides. Reports should feed into the existing SASC watch process and be formatted for inclusion in the President's Daily Brief if indicators reach crisis threshold. Ensure linguist support is allocated for Urdu, Punjabi, and Hindi communications intercepts. I'd like an initial collection plan briefed to leadership by end of next week.",
